      "writtenOn": "2026-07-20T11:05:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If so, do we still need to decrease created_vcpus if vcpu creation is failed in the middle? If we do that, it may cause duplicated vcpu_handle for the later created vcpu. If we don\u0027t, the actually allowed vcpu number will be smaller than KVM_MAX_VCPUS, but this seems an acceptable limitation?\n\nYeah, I already had a local implementation of my idea [*] but then I realized it would be racy because we use `created_vcpus` in a different way than the host KVM does...\n\nSo I came to the conclusion that the right way to validate duplicate vcpu_id is still to do that in `attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm()`, together with installing the vCPU in the vcpus array _after_ creating the vCPU (i.e. similarly to the host KVM).\n\nAs for the fact that it still wouldn\u0027t prevent undesired clearing of an existing vCPU\u0027s `pid_table` entry in aosp/4151696, I\u0027m thinking: that is not a security issue (it would only cause IPIv effectively disabled for that existing vCPU), so we can still merge aosp/4151696 as a temporary solution for now.\n\nIt seems the right solution (for the security issue fixed by aosp/4151696, and potentially for other similar subtle issues) is to prevent loading (and thus running) any vCPUs of a VM once at least one of its vCPUs is freed (and vice versa, prevent freeing a vCPU if at least one of other vCPUs of the same VM is loaded). And it seems it should be quite doable. But it seems it would require some refactoring of pkvm_vcpu_load() + pkvm_vcpu_put() + __pkvm_vcpu_free() + attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm() + detach_pkvm_vcpu_from_vm().\n\nSo for now I\u0027m just gonna add a FIXME for that to aosp/4151696.\n\n[*] Just for the record, it looked like this:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c\nindex 8b2a9ba5aa76..29b0c6e07d74 100644\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c\n@@ -257,19 +257,16 @@ static int attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm(struct pkvm_vm *pkvm_vm, struct pkvm_vcpu *pkv\n \n \tpkvm_spin_lock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n \n-\tif (kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus \u003d\u003d KVM_MAX_VCPUS) {\n-\t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n-\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n-\t}\n-\tvcpu_handle \u003d kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus++;\n+\tvcpu_handle \u003d pkvm_vcpu-\u003evcpu.vcpu_idx;\n+\tBUG_ON(vcpu_handle \u003e\u003d kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus);\n+\tBUG_ON(pkvm_vm-\u003evcpus[vcpu_handle] !\u003d pkvm_vcpu);\n+\n \tpkvm_vcpu-\u003evcpu.arch.pkvm.handle \u003d vcpu_handle;\n \tpkvm_vcpu-\u003epkvm_vm \u003d pkvm_vm;\n-\tpkvm_vm-\u003evcpus[vcpu_handle] \u003d pkvm_vcpu;\n+\tatomic_set(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003evcpu_refs[vcpu_handle], 1);\n \n \tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n \n-\tatomic_set(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003evcpu_refs[vcpu_handle], 1);\n-\n \treturn vcpu_handle;\n }\n \n@@ -552,10 +549,15 @@ static int __vcpu_create(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct fpstate\n \t\t       PKVM_VCPU_BASE_SIZE +\n \t\t       kvm_vcpu_sz;\n \tint cpu \u003d raw_smp_processor_id();\n-\tint ret;\n+\tint ret, i;\n \n \tpkvm_spin_lock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n \n+\tif (kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus \u003d\u003d KVM_MAX_VCPUS) {\n+\t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n+\t\treturn -ENOSPC;\n+\t}\n+\n \tret \u003d postponed_per_vm_setup(kvm);\n \tif (ret) {\n \t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n@@ -568,16 +570,27 @@ static int __vcpu_create(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct fpstate\n \t\treturn ret;\n \t}\n \n+\tvcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003d READ_ONCE(pkvm_vcpu-\u003eshared_vcpu-\u003evcpu_id);\n+\tif (vcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003c 0 || vcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003e\u003d kvm-\u003earch.max_vcpu_ids) {\n+\t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n+\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n+\t}\n+\tfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus; i++) {\n+\t\tif (pkvm_vm-\u003evcpus[i] \u0026\u0026\n+\t\t    pkvm_vm-\u003evcpus[i]-\u003evcpu.vcpu_id \u003d\u003d vcpu-\u003evcpu_id) {\n+\t\t\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n+\t\t\treturn -EEXIST;\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tvcpu-\u003evcpu_idx \u003d kvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus++;\n+\tpkvm_vm-\u003evcpus[vcpu-\u003evcpu_idx] \u003d pkvm_vcpu;\n+\n \tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n \n \tvcpu-\u003ekvm \u003d kvm;\n \t/* Set cpu to -1 to indicate it is not loaded on any CPU */\n \tvcpu-\u003ecpu \u003d -1;\n \n-\tvcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003d READ_ONCE(pkvm_vcpu-\u003eshared_vcpu-\u003evcpu_id);\n-\tif (vcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003c 0 || vcpu-\u003evcpu_id \u003e\u003d kvm-\u003earch.max_vcpu_ids)\n-\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n-\n \tvcpu-\u003earch.last_vmentry_cpu \u003d -1;\n \tvcpu-\u003earch.regs_avail \u003d ~0;\n \tvcpu-\u003earch.regs_dirty \u003d ~0;\n@@ -589,7 +602,7 @@ static int __vcpu_create(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct fpstate\n \t\t\tkern_pkvm_va(pkvm_vcpu-\u003eshared_vcpu-\u003earch.mci_ctl2_banks);\n \t\tret \u003d share_vcpu_mce_banks(vcpu);\n \t\tif (ret)\n-\t\t\treturn ret;\n+\t\t\tgoto decrement_vcpu;\n \t} else {\n \t\tvcpu-\u003earch.mce_banks \u003d unused;\n \t\tunused +\u003d KVM_MCE_SIZE;\n@@ -677,6 +690,10 @@ static int __vcpu_create(struct kvm *kvm, struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct fpstate\n \tunsetup_vcpu_lapic(vcpu);\n unshare_mce:\n \tunshare_vcpu_mce_banks(vcpu);\n+decrement_vcpu:\n+\tpkvm_spin_lock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n+\tkvm-\u003ecreated_vcpus--;\n+\tpkvm_spin_unlock(\u0026pkvm_vm-\u003elock);\n \treturn ret;\n }\n \ndiff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.h b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.h\nindex e87f5ec1cc29..e0247bdf992a 100644\n--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.h\n+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.h\n@@ -91,11 +91,11 @@ struct pkvm_vm {\n  * @vm: struct pkvm_vm pointer, evaluated multiple times. Don\u0027t use expressions.\n  *\n  * Iterates over all vCPUs in the VM, automatically skipping if vCPU pointer is\n- * NULL.\n+ * NULL or if vCPU is not attached to a VM.\n  */\n #define for_each_pkvm_guest_vcpu(i, _vcpu, vm)\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n \tfor ((i) \u003d 0; (i) \u003c (vm)-\u003ekvm.created_vcpus \u0026\u0026\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n-\t\t    