      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, and I actually agree with Sean\u0027s points. I replied in https://lore.kernel.org/kvm/al87Nh8fde9iAuXy@google.com/\n\nLooks like we\u0027ll end up using a bitmap like Vineeth originally suggested. And yeah, if upstream will also use a bitmap, we can simply use the same bitmap in pKVM\u0027s instance of `struct kvm`, i.e. without adding any extra fields.\n\nSince this lack of checking for duplicate vcpu_id is not causing any known pKVM security issues for now, I think I\u0027ll just abandon this patch and aosp/4180757 and just add a TODO to `__vcpu_create()` for now (until there is a final conclusion in upstream).",
